IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc27-s745-life-sentence.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, sections 745 to 745.52 (imprisonment for life: the sentence to be pronounced,
-- the information the judge states, persons under 18, recommendations by the jury, ineligibility for parole, multiple murders, manslaughter in certain circumstances).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
-- Layer 1: the law, objectively. Every top-level name begins with the label of its provision.
-- Answers are `MAYBE BOOLEAN` (or a MAYBE of a type): JUST FALSE only where the text says no in its own words, NOTHING elsewhere.
-- The kind of homicide offence is an input from section 231 (part ccc8). High treason is not a kind of homicide offence in the core, so it is its own input.
-- The matters a judge is told to have regard to in sections 745.4, 745.5 and 745.51(1) are for the judge and are not computed (NOTES.md, what the text does not answer).

§ `Section 745 -- Sentence of life imprisonment`

DECLARE `s 745 sentence` IS ONE OF
    `s 745(a) life, without eligibility for parole until twenty-five years of the sentence have been served`
    `s 745(b) life, without eligibility for parole until twenty-five years have been served (second degree murder after a previous murder)`
    `s 745(b.1) life, without eligibility for parole until twenty-five years have been served (second degree murder after a previous intentional killing under the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act)`
    `s 745(c) life, without eligibility for parole until at least ten years have been served, or the greater number substituted under section 745.4`
    `s 745(c.1) life, without eligibility for parole until at least 10 years have been served, or the greater number substituted under paragraph 745.52(1)(a)`
    `s 745(d) life, with normal eligibility for parole`
    `s 745.1 the sentence is fixed by section 745.1`

-- The sentence for each kind of homicide offence, taking the offence as proved. "Subject to section 745.1": a person under 18 at the time of a first degree murder,
-- a second degree murder or a manslaughter in the circumstances of paragraphs 236(2)(a) to (d) is sentenced under section 745.1.
-- src:16104 | 745 Subject to section 745.1, the sentence to be pronounced against a person who is to be sentenced to imprisonment for life shall be
-- src:16105 | (a) in respect of a person who has been convicted of high treason or first degree murder, that the person be sentenced to imprisonment for life without eligibility for parole until the person has served twenty-five years of the sentence;
-- src:16106 | (b) in respect of a person who has been convicted of second degree murder where that person has previously been convicted of culpable homicide that is murder, however described in this Act, that that person be sentenced to imprisonment for life without eligibility for parole until the person has served twenty-five years of the sentence;
-- src:16107 | (b.1) in respect of a person who has been convicted of second degree murder where that person has previously been convicted of an offence under section 4 or 6 of the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act that had as its basis an intentional killing, whether or not it was planned and deliberate, that that person be sentenced to imprisonment for life without eligibility for parole until the person has served twenty-five years of the sentence;
-- src:16108 | (c) in respect of a person who has been convicted of second degree murder, that the person be sentenced to imprisonment for life without eligibility for parole until the person has served at least ten years of the sentence or such greater number of years, not being more than twenty-five years, as has been substituted therefor pursuant to section 745.4;
-- src:16109 | (c.1) in respect of a person who has been convicted of manslaughter in the circumstances set out in any of paragraphs 236(2)(a) to (d), that the person be sentenced to imprisonment for life without eligibility for parole until the person has served at least 10 years of the sentence or the greater number of years, not being more than 25 years, that has been substituted for that 10 years under paragraph 745.52(1)(a); and
-- src:16110 | (d) in respect of a person who has been convicted of any other offence, that the person be sentenced to imprisonment for life with normal eligibility for parole.
@ref s 745 (src:16104-16110)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of homicide offence`
      `previously convicted of culpable homicide that is murder, however described in this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `previously convicted of an offence under section 4 or 6 of the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act that had as its basis an intentional killing, whether or not it was planned and deliberate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `convicted of manslaughter in the circumstances set out in any of paragraphs 236(2)(a) to (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `under the age of 18 at the time of the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 745 sentence`
`s 745 the sentence for the kind of homicide offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `first degree murder` THEN
        BRANCH
            IF `under the age of 18 at the time of the commission of the offence` THEN `s 745.1 the sentence is fixed by section 745.1`
            OTHERWISE `s 745(a) life, without eligibility for parole until twenty-five years of the sentence have been served`
    WHEN `second degree murder` THEN
        BRANCH
            IF `under the age of 18 at the time of the commission of the offence` THEN `s 745.1 the sentence is fixed by section 745.1`
            IF `previously convicted of culpable homicide that is murder, however described in this Act` THEN `s 745(b) life, without eligibility for parole until twenty-five years have been served (second degree murder after a previous murder)`
            IF `previously convicted of an offence under section 4 or 6 of the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act that had as its basis an intentional killing, whether or not it was planned and deliberate` THEN `s 745(b.1) life, without eligibility for parole until twenty-five years have been served (second degree murder after a previous intentional killing under the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act)`
            OTHERWISE `s 745(c) life, without eligibility for parole until at least ten years have been served, or the greater number substituted under section 745.4`
    WHEN `manslaughter` THEN
        BRANCH
            IF `convicted of manslaughter in the circumstances set out in any of paragraphs 236(2)(a) to (d)` AND `under the age of 18 at the time of the commission of the offence` THEN `s 745.1 the sentence is fixed by section 745.1`
            IF `convicted of manslaughter in the circumstances set out in any of paragraphs 236(2)(a) to (d)` THEN `s 745(c.1) life, without eligibility for parole until at least 10 years have been served, or the greater number substituted under paragraph 745.52(1)(a)`
            OTHERWISE `s 745(d) life, with normal eligibility for parole`
    WHEN `infanticide` THEN `s 745(d) life, with normal eligibility for parole`

-- src:16104 | 745 Subject to section 745.1, the sentence to be pronounced against a person who is to be sentenced to imprisonment for life shall be
-- src:16105 | (a) in respect of a person who has been convicted of high treason or first degree murder, that the person be sentenced to imprisonment for life without eligibility for parole until the person has served twenty-five years of the sentence;
-- src:16106 | (b) in respect of a person who has been convicted of second degree murder where that person has previously been convicted of culpable homicide that is murder, however described in this Act, that that person be sentenced to imprisonment for life without eligibility for parole until the person has served twenty-five years of the sentence;
-- src:16107 | (b.1) in respect of a person who has been convicted of second degree murder where that person has previously been convicted of an offence under section 4 or 6 of the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act that had as its basis an intentional killing, whether or not it was planned and deliberate, that that person be sentenced to imprisonment for life without eligibility for parole until the person has served twenty-five years of the sentence;
-- src:16108 | (c) in respect of a person who has been convicted of second degree murder, that the person be sentenced to imprisonment for life without eligibility for parole until the person has served at least ten years of the sentence or such greater number of years, not being more than twenty-five years, as has been substituted therefor pursuant to section 745.4;
-- src:16109 | (c.1) in respect of a person who has been convicted of manslaughter in the circumstances set out in any of paragraphs 236(2)(a) to (d), that the person be sentenced to imprisonment for life without eligibility for parole until the person has served at least 10 years of the sentence or the greater number of years, not being more than 25 years, that has been substituted for that 10 years under paragraph 745.52(1)(a); and
-- src:16110 | (d) in respect of a person who has been convicted of any other offence, that the person be sentenced to imprisonment for life with normal eligibility for parole.
@ref s 745 (src:16104-16110)
GIVEN `the person is to be sentenced to imprisonment for life` IS A BOOLEAN
      `convicted of high treason` IS A BOOLEAN
      `convicted of an offence that is neither high treason nor a kind of homicide offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 231 the kind of homicide offence` IS A MAYBE `Kind of homicide offence`
      `previously convicted of culpable homicide that is murder, however described in this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `previously convicted of an offence under section 4 or 6 of the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act that had as its basis an intentional killing, whether or not it was planned and deliberate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `convicted of manslaughter in the circumstances set out in any of paragraphs 236(2)(a) to (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `under the age of 18 at the time of the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 745 sentence`
`s 745 the sentence to be pronounced` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the person is to be sentenced to imprisonment for life`)
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the sentence to be pronounced against a person who is to be sentenced to imprisonment for life"
        IF `convicted of high treason`
        THEN JUST `s 745(a) life, without eligibility for parole until twenty-five years of the sentence have been served`   -- (a): section 745.1 does not name high treason
        IF `convicted of an offence that is neither high treason nor a kind of homicide offence`
        THEN JUST `s 745(d) life, with normal eligibility for parole`   -- (d): "any other offence"
        OTHERWISE `the sentence if the kind is known`
    WHERE
        `the sentence if the kind is known` MEANS
            CONSIDER `s 231 the kind of homicide offence`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): section 231 does not decide the kind of homicide offence on these facts
            WHEN JUST k THEN JUST (`s 745 the sentence for the kind of homicide offence` k `previously convicted of culpable homicide that is murder, however described in this Act` `previously convicted of an offence under section 4 or 6 of the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act that had as its basis an intentional killing, whether or not it was planned and deliberate` `convicted of manslaughter in the circumstances set out in any of paragraphs 236(2)(a) to (d)` `under the age of 18 at the time of the commission of the offence`)

-- The greater number of years, more than the minimum and not more than twenty-five, that a judge may substitute.
GIVEN substituted IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 745 the years when a greater number may be substituted for ten` MEANS
    CONSIDER substituted
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST 10   -- "at least ten years": the minimum, when no greater number has been substituted
    WHEN JUST n THEN
        IF n GREATER THAN 10 AND n AT MOST 25
        THEN JUST n
        ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such greater number of years, not being more than twenty-five"

-- src:16105 | (a) in respect of a person who has been convicted of high treason or first degree murder, that the person be sentenced to imprisonment for life without eligibility for parole until the person has served twenty-five years of the sentence;
-- src:16106 | (b) in respect of a person who has been convicted of second degree murder where that person has previously been convicted of culpable homicide that is murder, however described in this Act, that that person be sentenced to imprisonment for life without eligibility for parole until the person has served twenty-five years of the sentence;
-- src:16107 | (b.1) in respect of a person who has been convicted of second degree murder where that person has previously been convicted of an offence under section 4 or 6 of the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act that had as its basis an intentional killing, whether or not it was planned and deliberate, that that person be sentenced to imprisonment for life without eligibility for parole until the person has served twenty-five years of the sentence;
-- src:16108 | (c) in respect of a person who has been convicted of second degree murder, that the person be sentenced to imprisonment for life without eligibility for parole until the person has served at least ten years of the sentence or such greater number of years, not being more than twenty-five years, as has been substituted therefor pursuant to section 745.4;
-- src:16109 | (c.1) in respect of a person who has been convicted of manslaughter in the circumstances set out in any of paragraphs 236(2)(a) to (d), that the person be sentenced to imprisonment for life without eligibility for parole until the person has served at least 10 years of the sentence or the greater number of years, not being more than 25 years, that has been substituted for that 10 years under paragraph 745.52(1)(a); and
-- src:16110 | (d) in respect of a person who has been convicted of any other offence, that the person be sentenced to imprisonment for life with normal eligibility for parole.
@ref s 745 (src:16105-16110)
GIVEN sentence IS A `s 745 sentence`
      `the number of years substituted under section 745.4` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the number of years substituted under paragraph 745.52(1)(a)` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 745 the years of the sentence the person must serve before eligibility for parole` MEANS
    CONSIDER sentence
    WHEN `s 745(a) life, without eligibility for parole until twenty-five years of the sentence have been served` THEN JUST 25
    WHEN `s 745(b) life, without eligibility for parole until twenty-five years have been served (second degree murder after a previous murder)` THEN JUST 25
    WHEN `s 745(b.1) life, without eligibility for parole until twenty-five years have been served (second degree murder after a previous intentional killing under the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act)` THEN JUST 25
    WHEN `s 745(c) life, without eligibility for parole until at least ten years have been served, or the greater number substituted under section 745.4` THEN `s 745 the years when a greater number may be substituted for ten` `the number of years substituted under section 745.4`
    WHEN `s 745(c.1) life, without eligibility for parole until at least 10 years have been served, or the greater number substituted under paragraph 745.52(1)(a)` THEN `s 745 the years when a greater number may be substituted for ten` `the number of years substituted under paragraph 745.52(1)(a)`
    WHEN `s 745(d) life, with normal eligibility for parole` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): "normal eligibility for parole" is a matter of the Corrections and Conditional Release Act, and no number of years is stated here
    WHEN `s 745.1 the sentence is fixed by section 745.1` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the section): the years are those of section 745.1

§ `Section 745.01 -- Information in respect of parole`

-- src:16112 | 745.01 (1) Except where subsection 745.6(2) applies, at the time of sentencing under paragraph 745(a), (b) or (c), the judge who presided at the trial of the offender shall state the following, for the record:
@ref s 745.01(1) (src:16112)
GIVEN `the sentencing is under paragraph 745(a), (b) or (c)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection 745.6(2) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender is convicted of an offence committed on or after the day on which subsection 745.01(2) comes into force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge presided at the trial of the offender` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745.01(1) the judge shall state the information for the record` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `subsection 745.6(2) applies`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Except where subsection 745.6(2) applies" (fork F-13)
        IF `s 745.01(2) the exception applies: the offence was committed on or after the day the subsection comes into force` `the offender is convicted of an offence committed on or after the day on which subsection 745.01(2) comes into force`
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): subsection (2), "Subsection (1) does not apply if the offender is convicted of an offence committed on or after the day on which this subsection comes into force"
        IF NOT (`the sentencing is under paragraph 745(a), (b) or (c)`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at the time of sentencing under paragraph 745(a), (b) or (c)" (a duty whose "at the time of" is unmet, fork F-3)
        IF NOT (`the judge presided at the trial of the offender`)
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the judge who presided at the trial of the offender shall state"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- The words the judge states, as the text prints them.
-- src:16113 | The offender has been found guilty of (state offence) and sentenced to imprisonment for life. The offender is not eligible for parole until (state date). However, after serving at least 15 years of the sentence, the offender may apply under section 745.6 of the Criminal Code for a reduction in the number of years of imprisonment without eligibility for parole. If the jury hearing the application reduces the period of parole ineligibility, the offender may then make an application for parole under the Corrections and Conditional Release Act at the end of that reduced period.
@ref s 745.01(1) (src:16113)
`s 745.01(1) the statement the judge shall state` MEANS "The offender has been found guilty of (state offence) and sentenced to imprisonment for life. The offender is not eligible for parole until (state date). However, after serving at least 15 years of the sentence, the offender may apply under section 745.6 of the Criminal Code for a reduction in the number of years of imprisonment without eligibility for parole. If the jury hearing the application reduces the period of parole ineligibility, the offender may then make an application for parole under the Corrections and Conditional Release Act at the end of that reduced period."

-- Subsection (2): the exception, as the one fact it turns on. Subsection (1) calls it.
-- src:16115 | (2) Subsection (1) does not apply if the offender is convicted of an offence committed on or after the day on which this subsection comes into force.
@ref s 745.01(2) (src:16115)
GIVEN `the offender is convicted of an offence committed on or after the day on which subsection 745.01(2) comes into force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 745.01(2) the exception applies: the offence was committed on or after the day the subsection comes into force` MEANS
    `the offender is convicted of an offence committed on or after the day on which subsection 745.01(2) comes into force`

§ `Section 745.1 -- Persons under 18`

-- The years of a life sentence without eligibility for parole when the person was under 18 at the time of the offence.
-- src:16117 | 745.1 The sentence to be pronounced against a person who was under the age of 18 at the time of the commission of the offence for which the person was convicted of first degree murder, second degree murder or manslaughter in the circumstances set out in any of paragraphs 236(2)(a) to (d) and who is to be sentenced to imprisonment for life shall be that the person be sentenced to imprisonment for life without eligibility for parole until the person has served
-- src:16118 | (a) such period between five and seven years of the sentence as is specified by the judge presiding at the trial, or if no period is specified by the judge presiding at the trial, five years, in the case of a person who was under the age of sixteen at the time of the commission of the offence;
-- src:16119 | (b) ten years, in the case of a person convicted of first degree murder who was sixteen or seventeen years of age at the time of the commission of the offence; and
-- src:16120 | (c) seven years, in the case of a person who was convicted of second degree murder or of manslaughter in the circumstances set out in any of paragraphs 236(2)(a) to (d) and who was 16 or 17 years of age at the time of the commission of the offence.
@ref s 745.1 (src:16117-16120)
GIVEN `the age of the person at the time of the commission of the offence` IS A NUMBER
      `s 231 the kind of homicide offence` IS A MAYBE `Kind of homicide offence`
      `convicted of manslaughter in the circumstances set out in any of paragraphs 236(2)(a) to (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period between five and seven years specified by the judge presiding at the trial` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 745.1 the years without eligibility for parole` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the age of the person at the time of the commission of the offence` AT LEAST 18
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a person who was under the age of 18 at the time of the commission of the offence"
        IF `s 231 the kind of homicide offence` EQUALS NOTHING
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (undefined term): section 231 does not decide the kind of homicide offence on these facts
        OTHERWISE `the years for the kind`
    WHERE
        `the years for the kind` MEANS
            CONSIDER `s 231 the kind of homicide offence`
            WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
            WHEN JUST k THEN `s 745.1 the years for a person under 18 of the kind` `the age of the person at the time of the commission of the offence` k `convicted of manslaughter in the circumstances set out in any of paragraphs 236(2)(a) to (d)` `the period between five and seven years specified by the judge presiding at the trial`

GIVEN age IS A NUMBER
      kind IS A `Kind of homicide offence`
      `convicted of manslaughter in the circumstances set out in any of paragraphs 236(2)(a) to (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      specified IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 745.1 the years for a person under 18 of the kind` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `first degree murder` THEN
        BRANCH
            IF age LESS THAN 16 THEN `the years under sixteen`   -- (a)
            OTHERWISE JUST 10   -- (b): sixteen or seventeen, first degree murder
    WHEN `second degree murder` THEN
        BRANCH
            IF age LESS THAN 16 THEN `the years under sixteen`   -- (a)
            OTHERWISE JUST 7   -- (c): sixteen or seventeen, second degree murder
    WHEN `manslaughter` THEN
        BRANCH
            IF NOT (`convicted of manslaughter in the circumstances set out in any of paragraphs 236(2)(a) to (d)`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "manslaughter in the circumstances set out in any of paragraphs 236(2)(a) to (d)"
            IF age LESS THAN 16 THEN `the years under sixteen`   -- (a)
            OTHERWISE JUST 7   -- (c): sixteen or seventeen, manslaughter in those circumstances
    WHEN `infanticide` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section names first degree murder, second degree murder and manslaughter in those circumstances
    WHERE
        `the years under sixteen` MEANS
            CONSIDER specified
            WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST 5   -- (a): "if no period is specified by the judge presiding at the trial, five years"
            WHEN JUST n THEN
                IF n AT LEAST 5 AND n AT MOST 7
                THEN JUST n
                ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "such period between five and seven years ... as is specified" ("between" is read as including five and seven: fork F-8)

§ `Sections 745.2 to 745.3 -- Recommendation by the jury`

-- src:16122 | 745.2 Subject to section 745.3, where a jury finds an accused guilty of second degree murder, the judge presiding at the trial shall, before discharging the jury, put to them the following question:
@ref s 745.2 (src:16122)
GIVEN `the jury finds the accused guilty of second degree murder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 745.3 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge put the question to the jury before discharging the jury` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745.2 the judge has put the question to the jury as the section requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the jury finds the accused guilty of second degree murder`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where a jury finds an accused guilty of second degree murder" (a duty whose "where" is unmet, fork F-3)
        IF `section 745.3 applies`
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to section 745.3": the question for a person under sixteen is the one in section 745.3
        IF `the judge put the question to the jury before discharging the jury` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the judge presiding at the trial shall, before discharging the jury, put to them the following question"

-- src:16123 | You have found the accused guilty of second degree murder and the law requires that I now pronounce a sentence of imprisonment for life against the accused. Do you wish to make any recommendation with respect to the number of years that the accused must serve before the accused is eligible for release on parole? You are not required to make any recommendation but if you do, your recommendation will be considered by me when I am determining whether I should substitute for the ten year period, which the law would otherwise require the accused to serve before the accused is eligible to be considered for release on parole, a number of years that is more than ten but not more than twenty-five.
@ref s 745.2 (src:16123)
`s 745.2 the question the judge shall put` MEANS "You have found the accused guilty of second degree murder and the law requires that I now pronounce a sentence of imprisonment for life against the accused. Do you wish to make any recommendation with respect to the number of years that the accused must serve before the accused is eligible for release on parole? You are not required to make any recommendation but if you do, your recommendation will be considered by me when I am determining whether I should substitute for the ten year period, which the law would otherwise require the accused to serve before the accused is eligible to be considered for release on parole, a number of years that is more than ten but not more than twenty-five."

-- src:16125 | 745.21 (1) Where a jury finds an accused guilty of murder and that accused has previously been convicted of murder, the judge presiding at the trial shall, before discharging the jury, put to them the following question:
@ref s 745.21(1) (src:16125)
GIVEN `the jury finds the accused guilty of murder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused has previously been convicted of murder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge put the question to the jury before discharging the jury` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745.21(1) the judge has put the question to the jury as the subsection requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the jury finds the accused guilty of murder` AND `the accused has previously been convicted of murder`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a jury finds an accused guilty of murder and that accused has previously been convicted of murder" (a duty whose "where" is unmet, fork F-3)
        IF `the judge put the question to the jury before discharging the jury` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the judge presiding at the trial shall, before discharging the jury, put to them the following question"

-- src:16126 | You have found the accused guilty of murder. The law requires that I now pronounce a sentence of imprisonment for life against the accused. Do you wish to make any recommendation with respect to the period without eligibility for parole to be served for this murder consecutively to the period without eligibility for parole imposed for the previous murder? You are not required to make any recommendation, but if you do, your recommendation will be considered by me when I make my determination.
@ref s 745.21(1) (src:16126)
`s 745.21(1) the question the judge shall put` MEANS "You have found the accused guilty of murder. The law requires that I now pronounce a sentence of imprisonment for life against the accused. Do you wish to make any recommendation with respect to the period without eligibility for parole to be served for this murder consecutively to the period without eligibility for parole imposed for the previous murder? You are not required to make any recommendation, but if you do, your recommendation will be considered by me when I make my determination."

-- src:16128 | (2) Subsection (1) applies to an offender who is convicted of murders committed on a day after the day on which this section comes into force and for which the offender is sentenced under this Act, the National Defence Act or the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act.
@ref s 745.21(2) (src:16128)
GIVEN `the murders were committed on a day after the day on which section 745.21 comes into force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the offender is sentenced under this Act, the National Defence Act or the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745.21(2) subsection (1) applies to the offender` MEANS
    IF `the murders were committed on a day after the day on which section 745.21 comes into force` AND `the offender is sentenced under this Act, the National Defence Act or the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "applies to an offender who is convicted of murders committed on a day after the day on which this section comes into force and for which the offender is sentenced under this Act, the National Defence Act or the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act" (a scope limit with no "only", ruling (c))

-- src:16130 | 745.3 Where a jury finds an accused guilty of first degree murder or second degree murder and the accused was under the age of sixteen at the time of the commission of the offence, the judge presiding at the trial shall, before discharging the jury, put to them the following question:
@ref s 745.3 (src:16130)
GIVEN `the jury finds the accused guilty of first degree murder or second degree murder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the accused was under the age of sixteen at the time of the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge put the question to the jury before discharging the jury` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745.3 the judge has put the question to the jury as the section requires` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the jury finds the accused guilty of first degree murder or second degree murder` AND `the accused was under the age of sixteen at the time of the commission of the offence`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a jury finds an accused guilty of first degree murder or second degree murder and the accused was under the age of sixteen" (a duty whose "where" is unmet, fork F-3)
        IF `the judge put the question to the jury before discharging the jury` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the judge presiding at the trial shall, before discharging the jury, put to them the following question"

-- src:16131 | You have found the accused guilty of first degree murder (or second degree murder) and the law requires that I now pronounce a sentence of imprisonment for life against the accused. Do you wish to make any recommendation with respect to the period of imprisonment that the accused must serve before the accused is eligible for release on parole? You are not required to make any recommendation but if you do, your recommendation will be considered by me when I am determining the period of imprisonment that is between five years and seven years that the law would require the accused to serve before the accused is eligible to be considered for release on parole.
@ref s 745.3 (src:16131)
`s 745.3 the question the judge shall put` MEANS "You have found the accused guilty of first degree murder (or second degree murder) and the law requires that I now pronounce a sentence of imprisonment for life against the accused. Do you wish to make any recommendation with respect to the period of imprisonment that the accused must serve before the accused is eligible for release on parole? You are not required to make any recommendation but if you do, your recommendation will be considered by me when I am determining the period of imprisonment that is between five years and seven years that the law would require the accused to serve before the accused is eligible to be considered for release on parole."

§ `Sections 745.4 to 745.52 -- Ineligibility for parole`

DECLARE `s 745.4 judge` IS ONE OF
    `s 745.4 the judge who presided at the trial of the offender`
    `s 745.4 another judge of the same court`
    `s 745.4 a judge of another court`

-- A judge who may order: the presiding judge, or any judge of the same court if the presiding judge is unable to do so.
GIVEN judge IS A `s 745.4 judge`
      `the presiding judge is unable to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 745.4 the judge is one the sections allow to make the order` MEANS
    CONSIDER judge
    WHEN `s 745.4 the judge who presided at the trial of the offender` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 745.4 another judge of the same court` THEN `the presiding judge is unable to do so`
    WHEN `s 745.4 a judge of another court` THEN FALSE

-- src:16133 | 745.4 Subject to section 745.5, at the time of the sentencing under section 745 of an offender who is convicted of second degree murder, the judge who presided at the trial of the offender or, if that judge is unable to do so, any judge of the same court may, having regard to the character of the offender, the nature of the offence and the circumstances surrounding its commission, and to the recommendation, if any, made pursuant to section 745.2, by order, substitute for ten years a number of years of imprisonment (being more than ten but not more than twenty-five) without eligibility for parole, as the judge deems fit in the circumstances.
@ref s 745.4 (src:16133)
GIVEN `the sentencing is under section 745 of an offender who is convicted of second degree murder` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 745.5 applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      judge IS A `s 745.4 judge`
      `the presiding judge is unable to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
      years IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745.4 the judge may, by order, substitute for ten years a number of years of imprisonment without eligibility for parole` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the sentencing is under section 745 of an offender who is convicted of second degree murder`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at the time of the sentencing under section 745 of an offender who is convicted of second degree murder" (an "at the time of" gate on a "may", treated as a "where" gate: assumed, not ruled; see ruling (b); listed, group (i))
        IF `section 745.5 applies` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to section 745.5": for an offender under sixteen, section 745.5 decides
        IF NOT (`s 745.4 the judge is one the sections allow to make the order` judge `the presiding judge is unable to do so`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the judge who presided at the trial of the offender or, if that judge is unable to do so, any judge of the same court"
        IF years GREATER THAN 10 AND years AT MOST 25 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a number of years of imprisonment (being more than ten but not more than twenty-five)" (a grant named "may": fork F-2, the other reading is JUST FALSE)

-- src:16135 | 745.5 At the time of the sentencing under section 745.1 of an offender who is convicted of first degree murder or second degree murder and who was under the age of sixteen at the time of the commission of the offence, the judge who presided at the trial of the offender or, if that judge is unable to do so, any judge of the same court, may, having regard to the age and character of the offender, the nature of the offence and the circumstances surrounding its commission, and to the recommendation, if any, made pursuant to section 745.3, by order, decide the period of imprisonment the offender is to serve that is between five years and seven years without eligibility for parole, as the judge deems fit in the circumstances.
@ref s 745.5 (src:16135)
GIVEN `the sentencing is under section 745.1 of an offender who is convicted of first degree murder or second degree murder and who was under the age of sixteen at the time of the commission of the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      judge IS A `s 745.4 judge`
      `the presiding judge is unable to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
      years IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745.5 the judge may, by order, decide the period of imprisonment the offender is to serve without eligibility for parole` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the sentencing is under section 745.1 of an offender who is convicted of first degree murder or second degree murder and who was under the age of sixteen at the time of the commission of the offence`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "At the time of the sentencing under section 745.1 of an offender who is convicted of first degree murder or second degree murder and who was under the age of sixteen" (an "at the time of" gate on a "may", treated as a "where" gate: assumed, not ruled; see ruling (b); listed, group (i))
        IF NOT (`s 745.4 the judge is one the sections allow to make the order` judge `the presiding judge is unable to do so`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the judge who presided at the trial of the offender or, if that judge is unable to do so, any judge of the same court"
        IF years AT LEAST 5 AND years AT MOST 7 THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the period of imprisonment the offender is to serve that is between five years and seven years" (a grant named "may": fork F-2, the other reading is JUST FALSE; "between" read as including five and seven: fork F-8)

-- src:16137 | 745.51 (1) At the time of the sentencing under section 745 of an offender who is convicted of murder and who has already been convicted of one or more other murders, the judge who presided at the trial of the offender or, if that judge is unable to do so, any judge of the same court may, having regard to the character of the offender, the nature of the offence and the circumstances surrounding its commission, and the recommendation, if any, made pursuant to section 745.21, by order, decide that the periods without eligibility for parole for each murder conviction are to be served consecutively.
@ref s 745.51(1) (src:16137)
GIVEN `the sentencing is under section 745 of an offender who is convicted of murder and who has already been convicted of one or more other murders` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subsection (3) applies: the murders were committed on a day after the day on which section 745.51 comes into force, and the offender is sentenced under this Act, the National Defence Act or the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      judge IS A `s 745.4 judge`
      `the presiding judge is unable to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745.51(1) the judge may, by order, decide that the periods without eligibility for parole for each murder conviction are to be served consecutively` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the sentencing is under section 745 of an offender who is convicted of murder and who has already been convicted of one or more other murders`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "At the time of the sentencing under section 745 of an offender who is convicted of murder and who has already been convicted of one or more other murders" (an "at the time of" gate on a "may", treated as a "where" gate: assumed, not ruled; see ruling (b); listed, group (i))
        IF NOT (`s 745.51(3) subsections (1) and (2) apply: the murders were committed after the day the section comes into force, and the offender is sentenced under this Act, the National Defence Act or the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act` `subsection (3) applies: the murders were committed on a day after the day on which section 745.51 comes into force, and the offender is sentenced under this Act, the National Defence Act or the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act`)
        THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (3), "apply to an offender who is convicted of murders committed on a day after the day on which this section comes into force" (a scope limit with no "only", ruling (c))
        IF NOT (`s 745.4 the judge is one the sections allow to make the order` judge `the presiding judge is unable to do so`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the judge who presided at the trial of the offender or, if that judge is unable to do so, any judge of the same court"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:16139 | (2) The judge shall give, either orally or in writing, reasons for the decision to make or not to make an order under subsection (1).
@ref s 745.51(2) (src:16139)
GIVEN `the judge decides to make or not to make an order under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the judge gives reasons, either orally or in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745.51(2) the judge shall give reasons for the decision to make or not to make an order under subsection (1)` MEANS
    IF `the judge decides to make or not to make an order under subsection (1)` AND `the judge gives reasons, either orally or in writing`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The judge shall give, either orally or in writing, reasons for the decision to make or not to make an order under subsection (1)" (a duty not done) (fork F-14)

-- Subsection (3): the scope limit on (1) and (2), as the one fact it turns on. Subsection (1) calls it.
-- src:16141 | (3) Subsections (1) and (2) apply to an offender who is convicted of murders committed on a day after the day on which this section comes into force and for which the offender is sentenced under this Act, the National Defence Act or the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act.
@ref s 745.51(3) (src:16141)
GIVEN `subsection (3) applies: the murders were committed on a day after the day on which section 745.51 comes into force, and the offender is sentenced under this Act, the National Defence Act or the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 745.51(3) subsections (1) and (2) apply: the murders were committed after the day the section comes into force, and the offender is sentenced under this Act, the National Defence Act or the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act` MEANS
    `subsection (3) applies: the murders were committed on a day after the day on which section 745.51 comes into force, and the offender is sentenced under this Act, the National Defence Act or the Crimes Against Humanity and War Crimes Act`

DECLARE `s 745.52(1) sentencing` IS ONE OF
    `s 745.52(1)(a) a sentencing under paragraph 745(c.1)`
    `s 745.52(1)(b) a sentencing under paragraph 745.1(a)`
    `s 745.52(1) a sentencing of another kind`

-- src:16143 | 745.52 (1) At the time of sentencing under paragraph 745(c.1) or 745.1(a) of an offender who is convicted of manslaughter in the circumstances set out in any of paragraphs 236(2)(a) to (d), the judge who presided at the trial of the offender — or, if that judge is unable to do so, any judge of the same court — may, by order and as the judge considers fit in the circumstances,
-- src:16144 | (a) substitute for 10 years a greater number of years, of up to 25, of imprisonment without eligibility for parole, in the case of a sentencing under paragraph 745(c.1); or
-- src:16145 | (b) decide the period of imprisonment the offender is to serve that is between five and seven years without eligibility for parole, in the case of a sentencing under paragraph 745.1(a).
@ref s 745.52(1) (src:16143-16145)
GIVEN sentencing IS A `s 745.52(1) sentencing`
      `the offender is convicted of manslaughter in the circumstances set out in any of paragraphs 236(2)(a) to (d)` IS A BOOLEAN
      judge IS A `s 745.4 judge`
      `the presiding judge is unable to do so` IS A BOOLEAN
      years IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745.52(1) the judge may, by order, decide the number of years without eligibility for parole` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT (`the offender is convicted of manslaughter in the circumstances set out in any of paragraphs 236(2)(a) to (d)`)) OR (sentencing EQUALS `s 745.52(1) a sentencing of another kind`)
        THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "At the time of sentencing under paragraph 745(c.1) or 745.1(a) of an offender who is convicted of manslaughter in the circumstances set out in any of paragraphs 236(2)(a) to (d)" (an "at the time of" gate on a "may", treated as a "where" gate: assumed, not ruled; see ruling (b); listed, group (i))
        IF NOT (`s 745.4 the judge is one the sections allow to make the order` judge `the presiding judge is unable to do so`) THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "the judge who presided at the trial of the offender — or, if that judge is unable to do so, any judge of the same court"
        IF sentencing EQUALS `s 745.52(1)(a) a sentencing under paragraph 745(c.1)` AND years GREATER THAN 10 AND years AT MOST 25 THEN JUST TRUE   -- (a)
        IF sentencing EQUALS `s 745.52(1)(b) a sentencing under paragraph 745.1(a)` AND years AT LEAST 5 AND years AT MOST 7 THEN JUST TRUE   -- (b)
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(a) substitute for 10 years a greater number of years, of up to 25 ... (b) decide the period ... between five and seven years" (a grant named "may": fork F-2, the other reading is JUST FALSE; "between" read as including five and seven: fork F-8)

DECLARE `s 745.52(2) matter` IS ONE OF
    `s 745.52(2) the character of the offender`
    `s 745.52(2) the nature of the offence`
    `s 745.52(2) the circumstances surrounding the commission of the offence`
    `s 745.52(2) the age of the offender`
    `s 745.52(2) another matter`

-- src:16147 | (2) For the purposes of subsection (1), the judge shall have regard to the character of the offender, the nature of the offence and the circumstances surrounding its commission and, in respect of a decision under paragraph (1)(b), the age of the offender.
@ref s 745.52(2) (src:16147)
GIVEN matter IS A `s 745.52(2) matter`
      `the decision is under paragraph (1)(b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 745.52(2) the judge shall have regard to the matter` MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `s 745.52(2) the character of the offender` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 745.52(2) the nature of the offence` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 745.52(2) the circumstances surrounding the commission of the offence` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 745.52(2) the age of the offender` THEN (IF `the decision is under paragraph (1)(b)` THEN JUST TRUE ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of a decision under paragraph (1)(b), the age of the offender"
    WHEN `s 745.52(2) another matter` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "shall have regard to" names four matters and does not say "only"
